+# Staged Autonomy Runbook
+
+Purpose: Switch the platform between conservative, hybrid and aggressive autonomy modes safely.
+
+Prereqs:
+ - Orchestrator deployed and reading ops/config/autonomy_modes.yaml (or loaded as ConfigMap)
+ - OPA policies reviewed & signed by compliance
+ - Argo workflows deployed and tested in staging
+
+Switching mode (operator):
+ 1) Edit ConfigMap (or local file) and set desired mode (conservative|hybrid|aggressive).
+    kubectl -n aegis-system create configmap aegis-autonomy-modes --from-file=ops/config/autonomy_modes.yaml --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+ 2) Restart orchestrator deployment to reload config (or implement SIGHUP handler).
+    kubectl -n aegis-system rollout restart deployment aegis-orchestrator
+ 3) Verify current mode via Orchestrator health endpoint: curl http://aegis-orchestrator:8088/mode
+ 4) Run a smoke red-team incident in staging to validate behavior.
+
+Escalation:
+ - If false auto-remediations observed, immediately switch to conservative mode and open incident ticket.
+
+Audit:
+ - All mode switches must be recorded in the audit log and approved by Security lead.
